00:05:44.690 --> 00:05:45.280
Ah!

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:50.700
It's uncommon for non-Kumade people
to see a girl wearing a miko outfit, right?

00:05:50.700 --> 00:05:53.290
Wouldn't she be a pretty
good advertisement?

00:05:53.290 --> 00:05:53.870
Eh?

00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:56.290
Oh, yeah!

00:05:56.290 --> 00:05:57.830
Machi! That's it!

00:05:57.830 --> 00:06:00.040
I think that thoo-serou outfit is good.

00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:00.960
See-through.

00:06:01.420 --> 00:06:04.670
H-H-Hey, what're you saying, Hibiki-chan?!

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:04.670
H-H-Hey, what're you saying, Hibiki?!

00:06:05.170 --> 00:06:07.340
Nice idea, Hiiko!

00:06:07.340 --> 00:06:11.850
Machi, the village mascot girl,
dances with our specialties in her hands...

00:06:10.850 --> 00:06:12.600
No! No! No! No!

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:15.060
No! No! No! No! No!

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:15.060
This commercial will be popular for sure!

00:06:15.060 --> 00:06:17.480
No!

00:06:17.890 --> 00:06:20.440
Director, what do you think?

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:24.150
That's decided!

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:28.490
Well then, we're counting on you!

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:38.250
Hey, Machi...

00:06:38.250 --> 00:06:38.870
No.

00:06:39.790 --> 00:06:42.340
There's no way I'm doing that!

00:06:42.340 --> 00:06:43.920
Natsu should do it!

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:47.260
He's better suited to promote
Kumade Village, right?!

00:06:47.260 --> 00:06:48.880
I can't.

00:06:48.880 --> 00:06:50.180
I'm the cameraman.

00:06:50.180 --> 00:06:50.930
And a bear.

00:06:51.430 --> 00:06:52.800
Right.

00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:55.680
We can't reveal our village secret.

00:06:56.180 --> 00:07:00.270
Since I can't be onscreen, I'll contribute
to the project as a cameraman.

00:07:00.270 --> 00:07:05.480
Besides, "the village where bears roam" promotion
wouldn't make people want to come visit, would it?

00:07:00.480 --> 00:07:01.440
Think about it.

00:07:01.440 --> 00:07:03.230
Promoting ourselves as "the village where bears roam"

00:07:03.230 --> 00:07:05.480
wouldn't exactly make people want to come visit, would it?

00:07:07.740 --> 00:07:08.860
Please, Machi!

00:07:09.950 --> 00:07:10.780
What?

00:07:10.780 --> 00:07:12.370
We can't turn back now!

00:07:12.950 --> 00:07:15.080
You're the only one
who can save this village!

00:07:15.450 --> 00:07:16.370
Machi!

00:07:16.370 --> 00:07:18.160
You're the miko of Kumade Village...

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:18.870
No...

00:07:18.870 --> 00:07:21.330
You're the goddess of Kumade Village!

00:07:25.170 --> 00:07:28.880
To tell you the truth, I just threw
that idea out there at random earlier...

00:07:29.470 --> 00:07:32.640
...but I think... you look
good in a miko outfit.

00:07:33.140 --> 00:07:37.890
Also, Mr. Usui has been feeling down
for a while because of his sickness,

00:07:33.140 --> 00:07:37.890
Also, Usui-san has been feeling down
for a while because of his sickness,

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:42.140
so I think shooting it will probably remind him
of his young days and energize him!

00:07:45.060 --> 00:07:49.320
It's no exaggeration to say that
his recovery depends on you, Machi!

00:07:53.860 --> 00:07:54.780
I understand...

00:07:55.490 --> 00:07:57.280
But just once, okay?

00:07:59.250 --> 00:08:00.540
All right!

00:08:00.540 --> 00:08:01.500
Hiiko!

00:08:14.090 --> 00:08:17.390
Now that we have the heroine,
there's only issue left.

00:08:20.140 --> 00:08:22.850
If only we could solve that problem...

00:08:22.850 --> 00:08:24.020
"That problem"?

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:29.690
Well, it costs money to run
a 30-second commercial.

00:08:29.690 --> 00:08:30.690
Huh?

00:08:30.690 --> 00:08:31.650
What?!

00:08:32.280 --> 00:08:34.700
You didn't say a word about it earlier!

00:08:34.700 --> 00:08:36.070
Believe it or not, it costs...

00:08:38.620 --> 00:08:39.870
What?!

00:08:39.870 --> 00:08:42.000
Where do you get that kind of money?!

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:45.290
It's such a big amount, there's no way
the village office would have it.

00:08:45.290 --> 00:08:47.330
So I was wondering what to do.

00:08:47.330 --> 00:08:49.380
I can't believe you said,

00:08:49.380 --> 00:08:52.420
"It's been decided that our commercial
will air" without having money.

00:08:52.420 --> 00:08:54.680
We need a sponsor! A sponsor!

00:08:54.680 --> 00:08:56.640
Is there someone who can sponsor us?!

00:08:59.470 --> 00:09:01.680
Then how about old lady Tokuyama?

00:09:02.140 --> 00:09:04.390
Oh, the lady at the clocks and glasses shop?

00:09:04.390 --> 00:09:05.310
How come?

00:09:05.770 --> 00:09:08.230
Rumor says that she's been
saving up a pretty penny.

00:09:08.230 --> 00:09:10.520
They say that she's hiding it
behind the family altar.

00:09:11.070 --> 00:09:12.690
Who's your source?

00:09:12.940 --> 00:09:13.780
Okay then!

00:09:13.780 --> 00:09:16.280
I'll go talk to old lady Tokuyama!

00:09:19.070 --> 00:09:20.370
O-ho...

00:09:20.370 --> 00:09:23.160
That's quite a bit of money.

00:09:23.160 --> 00:09:24.410
Exactly!

00:09:24.410 --> 00:09:28.540
I thought you'd understand since
you love this village so much!

00:09:28.540 --> 00:09:29.670
Yep, yep.

00:09:29.670 --> 00:09:31.800
If many people visit Kumade Village,

00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:33.960
your shop will have tons of customers, too!

00:09:33.960 --> 00:09:35.170
Yep, yep.

00:09:35.170 --> 00:09:38.550
You'll have a booming business,
selling lots of clocks and glasses!

00:09:38.550 --> 00:09:39.970
Yep, yep.

00:09:39.970 --> 00:09:41.470
So please help us!

00:09:43.930 --> 00:09:45.390
Well...

00:09:48.270 --> 00:09:49.810
Please!

00:09:51.980 --> 00:09:53.280
Well, okay.

00:09:53.900 --> 00:09:55.950
I'll sponsor the commercial.

00:09:56.240 --> 00:09:57.780
Really?!

00:09:57.780 --> 00:09:58.950
But...

00:09:59.620 --> 00:10:03.450
I'll only pay... on one condition.

00:10:03.790 --> 00:10:05.960
A c-condition...?

00:10:06.370 --> 00:10:08.080
That's right.

00:10:11.250 --> 00:10:13.250
And... that condition is...?

00:10:29.980 --> 00:10:31.440
Whoa...

00:10:31.440 --> 00:10:35.990
A secluded hot spring
embraced by green mountains...

00:10:36.190 --> 00:10:39.110
What a wonderful location, Director!

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:41.410
All right, guys!

00:10:41.410 --> 00:10:43.450
Let's make a great commercial!

00:10:43.450 --> 00:10:45.120
Yeah!

00:10:48.620 --> 00:10:49.540
Yes?

00:10:49.540 --> 00:10:51.210
That roof is in the way?

00:10:51.210 --> 00:10:52.750
You want us to tear it down?

00:10:52.750 --> 00:10:54.800
Hey, there's no way we can't do that!

00:10:56.510 --> 00:10:58.090
He's acting like Director Kurosa—

00:11:00.180 --> 00:11:01.590
What's wrong, Machi?

00:11:02.090 --> 00:11:03.470
Hot spring...?

00:11:03.470 --> 00:11:04.560
Don't tell me...

00:11:03.550 --> 00:11:06.390
Could it possibly be me that's getting in there?

00:11:04.970 --> 00:11:06.560
I must get in there?

00:11:06.930 --> 00:11:08.140
Don't worry.

00:11:08.140 --> 00:11:09.440
They said that you could wear a swimsuit.

00:11:10.310 --> 00:11:11.600
Here, I brought it for you.

00:11:13.270 --> 00:11:14.980
I don't wanna do it after all!

00:11:14.980 --> 00:11:18.860
I can't show myself in a swimsuit nationwide!

00:11:19.280 --> 00:11:21.160
It'll only be aired locally.

00:11:21.160 --> 00:11:24.200
Be it nationwide or local, no means no!

00:11:21.240 --> 00:11:24.200
It doesn't matter whether it's nationwide or local... I said I don't wanna do it!

00:11:24.700 --> 00:11:27.290
It's time to give up, Machi.

00:11:27.290 --> 00:11:29.040
You accepted it once.

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:30.410
You should go all the way.

00:11:32.330 --> 00:11:33.580
Stupid Natsu...

00:11:34.250 --> 00:11:35.340
Let's see...

00:11:35.340 --> 00:11:40.050
First, Machi will appear carrying nameko,
a potato, and an apple and dancing!

00:11:40.050 --> 00:11:41.930
And then, she jumps into the hot spring!

00:11:41.930 --> 00:11:45.220
Next, Villager A says, "Slimy nameko."

00:11:42.430 --> 00:11:45.600
Nameko

00:11:45.220 --> 00:11:47.390
And Villager B says, "Hot and flaky potatoes."

00:11:45.600 --> 00:11:50.020
Potato

00:11:47.390 --> 00:11:48.350
Wow...

00:11:48.350 --> 00:11:50.350
So this is drawn by Mr. Usui, huh?

00:11:48.350 --> 00:11:50.350
So this is drawn by Usui-san, huh?

00:11:50.350 --> 00:11:51.730
He's pretty good.

00:11:51.730 --> 00:11:54.100
And then, Villager C says, "Crispy apples."

00:11:54.100 --> 00:11:57.190
And, at the end, Machi will have
a bite of the apple and says,

00:11:57.190 --> 00:11:59.280
"Kumade Village is the best!"

00:11:59.530 --> 00:12:00.280
Whoa!

00:12:00.280 --> 00:12:02.150
That sounds pretty good!

00:12:02.150 --> 00:12:04.740
Well then, let's see
who will do Villager A.

00:12:04.740 --> 00:12:07.410
Me! Me! Me! Me!

00:12:07.990 --> 00:12:10.290
Well then, we'll start auditions!

00:12:10.620 --> 00:12:13.500
Number one, Komatsu Kameji, 59 years old!

00:12:13.500 --> 00:12:15.670
My hobby is making and drinking doburoku!

00:12:15.540 --> 00:12:16.790
You don't have to talk about things like that.

00:12:15.670 --> 00:12:16.960
We don't need to know that.

00:12:17.420 --> 00:12:18.300
Well then...

00:12:18.670 --> 00:12:21.050
"Slimy nameko!"

00:12:24.890 --> 00:12:27.050
Try to express the sliminess more!

00:12:27.470 --> 00:12:28.720
Sliminess...?

00:12:29.310 --> 00:12:30.470
O-Okay.

00:12:30.810 --> 00:12:33.600
Slimy nameko! Slimy...! Slimy...!

00:12:33.640 --> 00:12:36.110
Slimy...! Slimy...! Slimy...!

00:12:34.730 --> 00:12:36.110
More passionately!

00:12:36.150 --> 00:12:37.440
Slimy! Slimy! Slimy! Slimy!

00:12:37.900 --> 00:12:39.730
Hot and flaky potatoes.

00:12:41.860 --> 00:12:44.070
Mom, act like a potato more!

00:12:44.070 --> 00:12:45.910
Hot and flaky potatoes.

00:12:46.450 --> 00:12:49.790
Mom, you're a potato from head to toe!

00:12:49.870 --> 00:12:51.500
Hot and flaky potatoes!

00:12:52.450 --> 00:12:54.290
Crispy apples!

00:12:55.000 --> 00:12:56.130
Okay, next person, please!

00:12:56.540 --> 00:12:57.670
What? That was it?

00:12:57.670 --> 00:12:59.710
Was it good? Or was it bad?

00:13:01.050 --> 00:13:02.550
Okay, then, here are the winners!

00:13:02.550 --> 00:13:04.550
Villager A is Hibiki.

00:13:04.550 --> 00:13:05.840
Why?!

00:13:05.840 --> 00:13:08.260
I wasn't in the audition!

00:13:08.260 --> 00:13:10.060
Director appointed you.

00:13:11.890 --> 00:13:14.100
You should let the person
who wants to do it do it.

00:13:14.810 --> 00:13:16.560
Next, Villager B is...

00:13:16.560 --> 00:13:17.400
Mom!

00:13:17.900 --> 00:13:19.190
All right!

00:13:19.190 --> 00:13:22.150
You were complimented highly on
your ability to act totally like a potato.

00:13:22.610 --> 00:13:24.280
And, Villager C is...

00:13:24.280 --> 00:13:25.360
Shota!

00:13:25.360 --> 00:13:26.410
Yay!

00:13:26.410 --> 00:13:27.280
That's all.

00:13:27.950 --> 00:13:30.870
Okay, then, shall we
start shooting now?!

00:13:31.450 --> 00:13:33.500
Machi, are you ready?

00:13:38.540 --> 00:13:40.630
You have nameko,
a potato and an apple?

00:13:41.130 --> 00:13:41.710
Yes.

00:13:42.670 --> 00:13:43.760
Also this...

00:13:44.130 --> 00:13:45.380
...these...

00:13:45.380 --> 00:13:46.340
...and this!

00:13:47.220 --> 00:13:48.300
What are these?!

00:13:48.300 --> 00:13:50.640
Well, they're like props.

00:13:51.100 --> 00:13:54.480
Oh, make sure that you don't get
the watch in the hot spring water, okay?

00:13:54.480 --> 00:13:55.890
O-Okay.

00:13:56.690 --> 00:14:00.480
Natsu, could you shoot zoomed in
on those watches and glasses?

00:14:00.860 --> 00:14:01.730
Why?

00:14:01.730 --> 00:14:02.900
Just a little bit is fine.

00:14:02.900 --> 00:14:03.440
Please!

00:14:04.900 --> 00:14:05.780
Okay.

00:14:06.280 --> 00:14:07.740
Everything's ready!

00:14:07.740 --> 00:14:09.280
Let's do it, Director!

00:14:10.410 --> 00:14:11.450
Scene one!

00:14:11.450 --> 00:14:13.450
"Dancing Machi with specialties in hands."

00:14:13.450 --> 00:14:14.540
Take one!

00:14:14.950 --> 00:14:16.790
Rea— Hm?

00:14:15.410 --> 00:14:19.790
Ready...

00:14:20.750 --> 00:14:22.880
Start!

00:14:25.920 --> 00:14:27.630
Machi, dance more!

00:14:29.300 --> 00:14:30.220
Yeah, like that!

00:14:30.220 --> 00:14:32.050
That's good! That's good!

00:14:32.050 --> 00:14:33.640
You look cute, Machi!

00:14:34.470 --> 00:14:35.890
Rub your face against the nameko!

00:14:35.720 --> 00:14:38.690
Wood Cultivated Nameko

00:14:36.890 --> 00:14:37.890
That's good!

00:14:38.640 --> 00:14:40.150
That's good!

00:14:40.730 --> 00:14:41.980
That's good!

00:14:42.440 --> 00:14:43.480
That's good!

00:14:43.480 --> 00:14:44.730
Hold on a sec!

00:14:45.190 --> 00:14:46.690
Cut!

00:14:46.690 --> 00:14:48.240
What's wrong, Machi?

00:14:48.700 --> 00:14:51.450
Don't I look like a stupid girl?

00:14:52.280 --> 00:14:52.780
What?

00:14:54.660 --> 00:14:55.790
Ahh! Ahhh!

00:14:55.790 --> 00:14:56.910
What's this awkward silence?!

00:14:57.330 --> 00:14:59.120
No, you don't!

00:14:59.120 --> 00:15:00.710
You looked cute!

00:15:00.710 --> 00:15:02.170
Right, Director?

00:15:05.210 --> 00:15:07.880
Can I... really trust them...?

00:15:08.920 --> 00:15:09.930
Scene two.

00:15:09.930 --> 00:15:11.590
"Slimy nameko," take one!

00:15:12.050 --> 00:15:14.180
Ready...

00:15:14.180 --> 00:15:16.350
Start!

00:15:17.600 --> 00:15:19.520
Slimy nameko.

00:15:19.520 --> 00:15:20.440
Hot and flaky pota—

00:15:19.520 --> 00:15:20.940
Crispy app—

00:15:21.400 --> 00:15:21.850
Ah!

00:15:22.400 --> 00:15:23.730
Cut!

00:15:24.400 --> 00:15:25.360
Take two!

00:15:26.280 --> 00:15:28.190
Slimy nameko!

00:15:28.190 --> 00:15:29.900
Hot and flaky potatoes.

00:15:29.900 --> 00:15:31.530
Crunchy apples!

00:15:31.530 --> 00:15:32.990
That's "Crispy apples"!

00:15:32.990 --> 00:15:33.450
Ah.

00:15:33.910 --> 00:15:35.200
Cut!

00:15:36.080 --> 00:15:37.620
Start!

00:15:40.580 --> 00:15:41.870
Kumade Village is the—

00:15:44.210 --> 00:15:45.630
Cut!

00:15:45.630 --> 00:15:47.050
It's a small bite!

00:15:47.050 --> 00:15:48.800
Swallow it and show your professionalism!

00:15:48.800 --> 00:15:50.170
I'm not a pro.

00:15:53.590 --> 00:15:55.260
Kumade Village is the best!

00:15:55.850 --> 00:15:57.180
Yep, it is!

00:15:56.100 --> 00:15:57.310
Yep, it is!

00:15:57.640 --> 00:15:59.390
Cut!

00:15:59.390 --> 00:16:01.190
All right, that was good!

00:16:03.100 --> 00:16:04.810
The last scene was perfect!

00:16:04.810 --> 00:16:07.020
Darn it, I wasn't in the commercial.

00:16:07.020 --> 00:16:08.900
That's a bummer.

00:16:09.610 --> 00:16:12.360
Well then, the shooting is over now!

00:16:12.360 --> 00:16:14.240
Good work, everyone!

00:16:14.240 --> 00:16:15.120
Hm?

00:16:17.580 --> 00:16:23.370
"It lacks impact... I wanna make a more
exciting, dynamic commercial..."?

00:16:23.830 --> 00:16:27.340
Well, it was all according to
the storyboards you created, Director.

00:16:29.550 --> 00:16:31.300
"Films are alive!"

00:16:31.300 --> 00:16:33.180
"Naturally, things can change
during the shooting."

00:16:33.760 --> 00:16:35.260
But it's too late.

00:16:35.260 --> 00:16:36.800
We've already finished shooting.

00:16:37.350 --> 00:16:40.850
Then... why don't we add a song?

00:16:41.140 --> 00:16:41.850
A song?

00:16:42.310 --> 00:16:43.390
To tell you the truth...

00:16:44.310 --> 00:16:46.980
I created a theme song for Kumade Village.

00:16:47.360 --> 00:16:51.150
Wouldn't it be fun to have us all
sing in the commercial?

00:16:51.150 --> 00:16:52.990
"We all" includes me, too?!

00:16:53.530 --> 00:16:56.280
Ku-Ku-Ku-Ku Kumade Village!

00:16:56.280 --> 00:16:59.700
It's a fun village where everyone is smiling.

00:17:01.200 --> 00:17:02.370
"That's it!"

00:17:02.830 --> 00:17:05.210
"That's indeed the passion
of Kumade Village!"

00:17:05.620 --> 00:17:07.130
Let's sing it!

00:17:07.130 --> 00:17:08.790
That sounds fun!

00:17:09.590 --> 00:17:13.380
We can shoot it, but we
don't have much time left.

00:17:13.920 --> 00:17:14.760
Okay!

00:17:15.260 --> 00:17:17.340
Then, guys, practice it right away!

00:17:17.340 --> 00:17:18.800
We'll shoot it in 30 minutes!

00:17:22.680 --> 00:17:25.230
Not much time is left,
so we can't make mistakes.

00:17:25.230 --> 00:17:26.400
Okay, guys?!

00:17:26.940 --> 00:17:28.980
"Kumade Village is a nice place," take one!

00:17:29.400 --> 00:17:31.150
No, I mean, this is a one-shot deal!

00:17:31.610 --> 00:17:34.280
Ready...

00:17:34.280 --> 00:17:36.570
Start!

00:17:37.700 --> 00:17:40.530
Ku-Ku-Ku-Ku Kumade Village!

00:17:40.530 --> 00:17:42.870
Kumade Village's specialties are...

00:17:42.870 --> 00:17:44.370
...slimy nameko...

00:17:44.370 --> 00:17:45.660
...hot and flaky potatoes, and...

00:17:45.660 --> 00:17:46.960
...crispy apples!

00:17:46.960 --> 00:17:49.210
Don't forget about my doburoku!

00:17:49.210 --> 00:17:52.130
Ku-Ku-Ku-Ku Kumade Village!

00:17:52.130 --> 00:17:54.630
Our even more amazing features are...

00:17:55.670 --> 00:18:00.850
...the village idol, who is
a cheerful, cute miko, and...

00:17:55.670 --> 00:18:00.850
...the village idol, who is
a cheerful, cute miko-san, and...

00:18:00.850 --> 00:18:03.560
...the joyful, fun villagers.

00:18:03.560 --> 00:18:04.810
Come and visit...

00:18:04.810 --> 00:18:06.060
Come and visit...

00:18:04.810 --> 00:18:06.060
Come and visit!

00:18:06.060 --> 00:18:06.810
Come and visit!

00:18:06.810 --> 00:18:07.560
Come and visit...

00:18:07.560 --> 00:18:11.360
...Kumade Village!

00:18:12.610 --> 00:18:14.940
Cut!

00:18:24.910 --> 00:18:25.700
Director?

00:18:30.830 --> 00:18:33.050
All right!

00:18:33.050 --> 00:18:34.840
We did it on the first try!

00:18:34.550 --> 00:18:36.840
I bet this commercial will be amazing!

00:18:34.840 --> 00:18:36.420
It's done for now...

00:18:48.140 --> 00:18:49.600
Oh, you're still working?

00:18:50.900 --> 00:18:53.730
I have to turn this in to
the TV station by tomorrow,

00:18:53.730 --> 00:18:55.030
so I'm editing the video right now.

00:18:55.530 --> 00:18:56.360
I see.

00:18:56.360 --> 00:18:57.150
Let me see.

00:18:57.150 --> 00:18:58.990
Do I look okay?

00:18:58.990 --> 00:19:00.320
Oh, you can't see it!

00:19:00.320 --> 00:19:02.320
It's not done yet.

00:19:02.320 --> 00:19:03.530
What's the problem?

00:19:03.530 --> 00:19:04.700
Let me see.

00:19:04.700 --> 00:19:05.830
No!

00:19:05.830 --> 00:19:09.250
I guess I'll save the fun
until the actual broadcast then.

00:19:09.710 --> 00:19:10.370
Well then...

00:19:10.370 --> 00:19:11.830
Don't work too hard.

00:19:12.330 --> 00:19:13.340
Okay!

00:19:15.880 --> 00:19:18.260
Now the important part starts here...

00:19:18.630 --> 00:19:21.130
Kumade Village's specialties are...

00:19:21.130 --> 00:19:22.390
...slimy nameko...

00:19:22.390 --> 00:19:23.760
...hot and flaky potatoes, and...

00:19:23.760 --> 00:19:24.930
...crispy apples!

00:19:24.930 --> 00:19:27.220
Don't forget about my doburoku!

00:19:32.230 --> 00:19:36.480
The weather forecast for the Tohoku region is next.

00:19:35.940 --> 00:19:38.440
Old man Usui is wearing a tuxedo.

00:19:38.440 --> 00:19:39.360
You can't blame him.

00:19:39.360 --> 00:19:41.030
This was his first work as a director.

00:19:41.820 --> 00:19:43.320
Wh-What am I gonna do?

00:19:43.320 --> 00:19:45.580
I'm so nervous that I can't look at the TV.

00:19:45.580 --> 00:19:46.790
Don't worry.

00:19:46.790 --> 00:19:49.120
Thirty seconds will pass in no time.

00:19:49.620 --> 00:19:51.040
It'll start soon!

00:19:51.580 --> 00:19:52.250
Four!

00:19:52.710 --> 00:19:56.250
Three! Two! One!

00:19:57.840 --> 00:20:00.590
Ku-Ku-Ku-Ku Kumade Village!

00:20:00.590 --> 00:20:03.010
Kumade Village's specialties are...

00:20:03.010 --> 00:20:04.260
...slimy nameko...

00:20:04.260 --> 00:20:05.640
...hot and flaky potatoes, and...

00:20:05.640 --> 00:20:06.810
...crispy apples!

00:20:06.850 --> 00:20:09.270
Don't forget Tokuyama Machiko!

00:20:09.270 --> 00:20:12.020
Ku-Ku-Ku-Ku Kumade Village!

00:20:10.310 --> 00:20:12.020
I got cut out!

00:20:12.020 --> 00:20:14.770
Our even more amazing features are...

00:20:15.860 --> 00:20:20.940
...the village idol, who is
a cheerful, cute Machi, and...

00:20:15.860 --> 00:20:20.940
...the village idol, who is
a cheerful, cute Machi-chan, and...

00:20:20.940 --> 00:20:23.570
...her joyful, fun Grandma.

00:20:23.570 --> 00:20:24.820
Come and visit...

00:20:24.820 --> 00:20:26.070
Come and visit...

00:20:24.820 --> 00:20:26.070
Come and visit!

00:20:26.070 --> 00:20:26.830
Come and visit!

00:20:26.830 --> 00:20:27.580
Come and visit...

00:20:27.580 --> 00:20:30.160
...Kumade Village...

00:20:30.160 --> 00:20:32.620
...to go to Tokuyama Clocks and Glasses!

00:20:33.830 --> 00:20:35.210
Here's the news for this afternoon.

00:20:35.790 --> 00:20:39.840
Regarding the missing Niwako and Toritaro,
the chickens that ran away from the chicken coop

00:20:39.840 --> 00:20:44.550
in Sannou Daisan Elementary
School's backyard yesterday...

00:20:44.550 --> 00:20:48.140
Well... 30 seconds just flew by, huh?

00:20:49.600 --> 00:20:50.970
Hey, Yoshio...!

00:20:50.970 --> 00:20:54.810
You call this a commercial
for Kumade Village?!

00:20:54.810 --> 00:20:56.860
I didn't have a choice!

00:20:56.860 --> 00:20:58.150
Old lady Tokuyama

00:20:58.150 --> 00:21:02.110
made it a condition that we advertise her shop and
play her granddaughter's song for her sponsorship!

00:21:02.110 --> 00:21:05.200
That was nothing but a commercial
for Tokuyama Clocks!

00:21:05.200 --> 00:21:06.410
That was fun!

00:21:06.780 --> 00:21:10.200
My part got cut, but you could hear
my voice in the song, right?

00:21:10.200 --> 00:21:11.200
Right?!

00:21:11.200 --> 00:21:14.290
It's strange to see yourself on TV, isn't it?

00:21:15.580 --> 00:21:18.290
It was just for a bit,
but I'm glad I showed up.

00:21:18.290 --> 00:21:20.170
Hurray for the commercial!

00:21:20.170 --> 00:21:21.340
Hurray!

00:21:22.670 --> 00:21:23.420
What?

00:21:24.260 --> 00:21:27.050
I wonder if this can really be
an advertisement for the village.

00:21:27.510 --> 00:21:29.010
I don't know.

00:21:29.970 --> 00:21:33.680
But... everyone seems to be
happy with it, so it's good, right?

00:21:34.980 --> 00:21:41.020
Th-Th... Th-Th-This...

00:21:43.400 --> 00:21:48.910
...isn't my work!

00:21:49.410 --> 00:21:50.330
He spoke.

00:21:57.500 --> 00:22:01.000
Oh, no! Old man Usui collapsed again!

00:22:01.460 --> 00:22:03.090
Ambulance! Ambulance!

00:22:03.090 --> 00:22:04.800
Call them! Call them!

00:22:05.760 --> 00:22:07.090
Ah, there's no reception.

00:23:37.970 --> 00:23:42.770
...Kumade Village, to go to
Tokuyama Clocks and Glasses!

00:23:43.100 --> 00:23:44.230
Okay, that was good!

00:23:44.230 --> 00:23:45.650
But let's try one more time!

00:23:46.270 --> 00:23:47.860
I bet everyone's gonna be upset...

00:23:50.280 --> 00:23:53.990
Kumamiko.
